  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Candesartan Cilexetil may be associated with Hypertension through off-label use in the context of Diastolic Heart Failure. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, where Candesartan Cilexetil is linked to Diastolic Heart Failure, which in turn is used off-label for other indications, including Hypertension. The off-label use of Candesartan Cilexetil in the treatment of Diastolic Heart Failure appears to be a potential mechanism through which it may be repurposed for Hypertension. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.6196) indicate a strong level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence highlights the importance of considering off-label use in drug repurposing, as it can provide alternative therapeutic pathways for conditions where standard indications are not applicable.",
